        "raw": "<p>So my group got into an argument over this last night. We&#39;ve only played a few times (and love the game), so I figured I would ask here to see what the proper play should have been.</p><p>During the Environment turn the card &quot;Atlantean Font of Power&quot; was played.&nbsp;</p><blockquote><p><span data-sheets-userformat=\"[null,null,12992,null,null,null,null,null,null,0,1,null,0,null,null,&quot;calibri,arial,sans,sans-serif&quot;,11]\" data-sheets-value=\"[null,2,&quot;At the end of the Environment turn, play the top card of the Villain deck. Play the top card of each Hero deck in turn order. If the played card is a Limited card already in play, discard that card and play the next card.\\nAt the start of the Environment turn, destroy this card.&quot;]\" style=\"font-size: 110%; font-family: calibri, arial, sans, sans-serif;\">At the end of the Environment turn, play the top card of the Villain deck. Play the top card of each Hero deck in turn order. If the played card is a Limited card already in play, discard that card and play the next card.<br />At the start of the Environment turn, destroy this card.</span></p></blockquote><p>Our Mr. Fixer character pulled from the top of his deck &quot;Overdrive&quot;</p><blockquote><p><span data-sheets-userformat=\"[null,null,15040,null,null,null,null,null,null,0,1,null,0,null,[null,2,0],&quot;calibri,arial,sans,sans-serif&quot;,11]\" data-sheets-value=\"[null,2,&quot;You may use Mr. Fixer's \\&quot;Strike\\&quot; power twice this turn.&quot;]\" style=\"font-size: 110%; font-family: calibri, arial, sans, sans-serif;\">You may use Mr. Fixer&#39;s &quot;Strike&quot; power twice this turn.</span></p></blockquote><p>The argument was split, with Mr. Fixer taking this interaction to mean that he can immediately use his Strike power twice now (during the Environment &#39;Play an Environment Card&#39; phase). His argument was that the card &quot;Atlantean Font of Power&quot; is designed to help the heroes get a boost on the villian/environment by giving them an extra card play, and that his &quot;Overdrive&quot; card meant he could use his Strike power now, not once, but twice, because &quot;Overdrive&quot; told him to.</p><p>I felt that this was incorrect, and that what actually should happen is nothing; Overdrive just allows Mr. Fixer to use his Strike power a second time when he could normally use a power, but since it was not that phase of the turn, he could actually do nothing right now (the card was essentially a &#39;dead card&#39;). My argument was that normally, Overdrive would be played during his Play a Hero Card phase, and would simply give him an extra use of his Strike power when he reached the Use a Hero Power phase. Since we were already passed that point, during a time when he could not normally use a power, that he cannot use a power, let alone twice. If the card had said something like &quot;Use the &#39;Strike&#39; power twice now&quot;, then it would work the way he had described.&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>So my question is, what would be the correct resolution of this situation? Was Mr. Fixer right? Was I right? Were we both wrong, and it should have a different result?</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Thanks in advance!</p>",
