      {
        "id": 146041,
        "name": "Pydro",
        "username": "Pydro",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/pydro/{size}/1844_2.png",
        "created_at": "2015-08-10T23:08:00.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Mr. Fixer would get to use Strike twice on the Environment's turn.</p>\n<p>Here are the rules for using powers outside of your turn:</p>\n<p>[quote=“<a href=\"https://greaterthangames.com/comment/89579#comment-89579\">MigrantP</a>”]</p>\n<p>This came up during development and we could not find any official ruling. It is working as we discussed with Christopher. Here is the logic, which also generalizes to \"play an additional card\" and \"draw an additional card\" text:\n</p><p>If the card granting an additional power use is played on a turn other than the card’s owner’s turn, then they immediately get to use a power. If they do not do it immediately, it's gone.\n</p><p>If the card granting an additional power use is played on the card's owner's turn,&nbsp;<strong>after</strong>&nbsp;the use power phase,&nbsp;then they immediately to use a power. If they do not do it immediately, it's gone.\n</p><p>If the card granting an additional power use is played on the card's owner's turn,&nbsp;<strong>before</strong>&nbsp;the use power phase,&nbsp;then must wait until their use power phase to use the additional power. (this is the typical use case, BTW)\n</p><p>\n[/quote]\n</p><p>FWIW, I agree with you logic, as you can see from the first post in that thread. However, it is incorrect.</p>",
        "post_number": 2,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T04:23:54.000Z",
