        "raw": "Mr. Fixer would get to use Strike twice on the Environment&#39;s turn.\n\nHere are the rules for using powers outside of your turn:\n\n[quote=\"<a href=\"https://greaterthangames.com/comment/89579#comment-89579\">MigrantP</a>\"]\n\n<p style=\"margin: 0px 10px 20px 0px; color: rgb(51, 51, 51); font-family: 'Open Sans', HelveticaNeue, 'Helvetica Neue', Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 14.3999996185303px; line-height: 21.5999984741211px; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\">This came up during development and we could not find any official ruling. It is working as we discussed with Christopher. Here is the logic, which also generalizes to &quot;play an additional card&quot; and &quot;draw an additional card&quot; text:\n<p style=\"margin: 0px 10px 20px 0px; color: rgb(51, 51, 51); font-family: 'Open Sans', HelveticaNeue, 'Helvetica Neue', Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 14.3999996185303px; line-height: 21.5999984741211px; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\">If the card granting an additional power use is played on a turn other than the card&rsquo;s owner&rsquo;s turn, then they immediately get to use a power. If they do not do it immediately, it&#39;s gone.\n<p style=\"margin: 0px 10px 20px 0px; color: rgb(51, 51, 51); font-family: 'Open Sans', HelveticaNeue, 'Helvetica Neue', Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 14.3999996185303px; line-height: 21.5999984741211px; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\">If the card granting an additional power use is played on the card&#39;s owner&#39;s turn,&nbsp;<strong>after</strong>&nbsp;the use power phase,&nbsp;then they immediately to use a power. If they do not do it immediately, it&#39;s gone.\n<p style=\"margin: 0px 10px 20px 0px; color: rgb(51, 51, 51); font-family: 'Open Sans', HelveticaNeue, 'Helvetica Neue', Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 14.3999996185303px; line-height: 21.5999984741211px; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\">If the card granting an additional power use is played on the card&#39;s owner&#39;s turn,&nbsp;<strong>before</strong>&nbsp;the use power phase,&nbsp;then must wait until their use power phase to use the additional power. (this is the typical use case, BTW)\n<p style=\"margin: 0px 10px 20px 0px; color: rgb(51, 51, 51); font-family: 'Open Sans', HelveticaNeue, 'Helvetica Neue', Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 14.3999996185303px; line-height: 21.5999984741211px; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\">\n[/quote]\n\n<p style=\"margin: 0px 10px 20px 0px; color: rgb(51, 51, 51); font-family: 'Open Sans', HelveticaNeue, 'Helvetica Neue', Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 14.3999996185303px; line-height: 21.5999984741211px; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\">FWIW, I agree with you logic, as you can see from the first post in that thread. However, it is incorrect.\n",
