      {
        "id": 146044,
        "name": "Arcanist Lupus",
        "username": "Arcanist_Lupus",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/arcanist_lupus/{size}/2169_2.png",
        "created_at": "2015-08-11T00:37:40.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Yes, although it's worth noting that you have to use the non-Strike power first.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Basically, the game is watching two things:</p>\n<p>Has Mr. Fixer used a power this power phase? &nbsp;If no, then he may use a power.</p>\n<p>Has Mr. Fixer used the Strike power twice this turn? &nbsp;If no, then he may use Strike.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>So if you use Strike, then the first condition and half the second condition are fulfilled, and you cannot use any power except for your second Strike. &nbsp;But if you use a different power first (which is possible because Overdrive doesn't say that you <span class=\"bbcode-i\">must</span> use Strike), then the second condition hasn't been fulfilled at all, so you can still Strike twice.</p>",
        "post_number": 5,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T04:23:54.254Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
