        "bookmarked": false,
        "raw": "Yes, although it&#39;s worth noting that you have to use the non-Strike power first.\n\n&nbsp;\n\nBasically, the game is watching two things:\n\nHas Mr. Fixer used a power this power phase? &nbsp;If no, then he may use a power.\n\nHas Mr. Fixer used the Strike power twice this turn? &nbsp;If no, then he may use Strike.\n\n&nbsp;\n\nSo if you use Strike, then the first condition and half the second condition are fulfilled, and you cannot use any power except for your second Strike. &nbsp;But if you use a different power first (which is possible because Overdrive doesn&#39;t say that you [i]must[/i] use Strike), then the second condition hasn&#39;t been fulfilled at all, so you can still Strike twice.\n",
