        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/chartype/{size}/2240_2.png",
        "created_at": "2015-08-11T01:21:06.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>As other's have said, Mr. Fixer's player was right, per the official ruling. I see your logic, but personally I would argue that this fits with how it's worded. Overdrive just says he can use \"strike\" twice this turn, it doesn't say that it must be when he could normally use a power. If it said \"during his power phase\", then I would agree with your argument.</p><p>If you have any more rules arguments in the future, you can refer to the list of official rules clarifications at&nbsp;http://www.spiffworld.com/sotm/files/sotm_rules_and_clarifications.pdf. Hope this helps!</p>",
        "post_number": 6,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T04:23:54.324Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
        "quote_count": 0,
        "incoming_link_count": 0,
        "reads": 0,
        "readers_count": 0,
        "score": 0.0,
        "yours": false,
        "topic_id": 13402,
        "topic_slug": "overdrive-atlantean-font-of-power",
        "display_username": "CharType",
        "primary_group_name": null,
        "flair_name": null,
        "flair_url": null,
        "flair_bg_color": null,
        "flair_color": null,
        "flair_group_id": null,
        "badges_granted": [],
        "version": 1,
        "can_edit": false,
