      {
        "id": 146046,
        "name": "Ameena",
        "username": "Ameena",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/ameena/{size}/1907_2.png",
        "created_at": "2015-08-11T13:38:55.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Similarly, if you look at Unity's golems, they all say they cannot be played \"during your play phase\". So if it's any other phase <span class=\"bbcode-i\">except</span> your Play phase (across any deck in that game) and something lets you play a card - go for it. It's why Unity loves characters like the Adept :D. The Overdrive thing with Fixer is exactly the same - it says that you may use Strike twice <span class=\"bbcode-i\">this</span> turn - it doesn't say it has to be <span class=\"bbcode-i\">your</span> turn, just whichever turn it happens to be right now ;).</p>",
        "post_number": 7,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T04:23:54.391Z",
